<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 29 May, from 1453 to 1999.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1453">1453 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">573 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantinople falls to the Ottoman Turks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a 53-day siege, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>'s army broke through the city walls; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos">Constantine XI</a> died in the fighting. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> ended, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> became the Ottoman capital.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1660">1660 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">366 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles II enters London as the monarchy is restored</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his 30th birthday, Charles II rode into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> to cheering crowds after years of exile. The Restoration ended the republican experiment that had followed his father's execution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1736">1736 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">290 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Patrick Henry is born in Virginia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patrick-henry">Patrick Henry</a> became one of the most powerful orators of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>. His 1775 speech ending 'Give me liberty, or give me death!' rallied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> to arm.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wisconsin becomes the 30th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a> joined the Union from the old Northwest Territory. It later became known for dairy farming and as a centre of the Progressive movement.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hillary and Tenzing reach the summit of Everest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-hillary">Edmund Hillary</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenzing-norgay">Tenzing Norgay</a>, a Sherpa from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, became the first climbers confirmed to have reached the summit of the world's highest mountain.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1999">1999 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">27 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nigeria returns to civilian rule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Olusegun Obasanjo was sworn in as president, ending fifteen years of military government. The date was kept as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>'s Democracy Day until 2019, when it moved to 12 June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li></ol>
